ding.o¤␀␀␀␀€–How much of the lookup texture will contribute to the color grading effect.o¤␀␀␀␀€èUse "Gaussian" for a faster but non physical depth of field; "Bokeh" for a more realistic but slower depth of field.o¤␀␀␀␀\The distance at which the blurring will start.o¤␀␀␀␀€‚The distance at which the blurring will reach its maximum radius.o¤␀␀␀␀€´The maximum radius of the gaussian blur. Values above 1 may show under-sampling artifacts.o¤␀␀␀␀€²Use higher quality sampling to reduce flickering and improve the overall blur smoothness.o¤␀␀␀␀FThe distance to the point of focus.o¤␀␀␀␀€æThe ratio of aperture (known as f-stop or f-number). The smaller the value is, the shallower the depth of field is.o¤␀␀␀␀€ÒThe distance between the lens and the film. The larger the value is, the shallower the depth of field is.o¤␀␀␀␀<The number of aperture blades.o¤␀␀␀␀,The curvature of aperture blades. The smaller the value is, the more visible aperture blades are. A value of 1 will make the bokeh perfectly circular.o¤␀␀␀␀VThe rotation of aperture blades in degrees.o¤␀␀␀␀€ÄThe type of grain to use. You can select a preset or provide your own texture by selecting Custom.o¤␀␀␀␀xUse the slider to set the strength of the Film Grain effect.o¤␀␀␀␀€ÚControls the noisiness response curve based on scene luminance. Higher values mean less noise in light areas.o¤␀␀␀␀€¸A tileable texture to use for the grain. The neutral value is 0.5 where no grain is applied.o¤␀␀␀␀0Total distortion amount.o¤␀␀␀␀€žIntensity multiplier on X axis. Set it to 0 to disable distortion on this axis.o¤␀␀␀␀€žIntensity multiplier on Y axis. Set it to 0 to disable distortion on this axis.o¤␀␀␀␀rDistortion center point. 0.5,0.5 is center of the screen.o¤␀␀␀␀€ôControls global screen scaling for the distortion effect. Use this to hide the screen borders when using high "Intensity."o¤␀␀␀␀€êThe motion blur technique to use. If you don't need object motion blur, CameraOnly will result in better performance.o¤␀␀␀␀€ØThe quality of the effect. Lower presets will result in better performance at the expense of visual quality.o¤␀␀␀␀€˜The strength of the motion blur filter. Acts as a multiplier for velocities.o¤␀␀␀␀RSets the maximum length, as a fraction of the screen's full resolution, that the velocity resulting from Camera rotation can have. Lower values will improve performance.o¤␀␀␀␀6Panini projection distance.o¤␀␀␀␀<Panini projection crop to fit.±Š␀␀␀␀␀r¤␀␀␀␀Flares±Š␀␀␀␀␀±Š␀␀␀␀␀r¤␀␀␀␀StreaksX¦␀␀±Š␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀r¤␀␀␀␀(Chromatic Abberationr¤␀␀o¤␀␀␀␀Shadow Limits␀␀vStart point of the transition between shadows and midtones.o¤␀␀␀␀rEnd point of the transition between shadows and midtones.r¤␀␀o¤␀␀␀␀ Highlight Limits␀␀|Start point of the transition between midtones and highlights.o¤␀␀␀␀xEnd point of the transition between midtones and highlights.o¤␀␀␀␀:The color to use for shadows.o¤␀␀␀␀@The color to use for highlights.o¤␀␀␀␀rBalance between the colors in the highlights and shadows.o¤␀␀␀␀€ˆSelect a tonemapping algorithm to use for the color grading process.±Š␀␀o¤␀␀␀␀␀␀␀€ÌSpecifies the range reduction mode used when HDR output is enabled and Neutral tonemapping is enabled.o¤␀␀␀␀JUse the ACES preset for HDR displays.o¤␀␀␀␀Specify how much hue to preserve. Values closer to 0 are likely to preserve hue. As values get closer to 1, Unity doesn't correct hue shifts.o¤␀␀␀␀\Enable to use values detected from the output device as paper white. When enabled, output images might differ between SDR and HDR. For best accuracy, set this value manually.o¤␀␀␀␀zThe reference brightness of a paper white surface. This property determines the maximum brightness of UI. The brightness of the scene is scaled relative to this value. The value is in nits.o¤␀␀␀␀4Enable to use the minimum and maximum brightness values detected from the output device. For best accuracy, considering calibrating 